# Architecture Reference

## Current Focus

The active teacher architecture focus is in `teacher.py`: MNIST data -> `HeavyEncoder` -> learned `linear` channel layer -> `HeavyRxDecoder`, then physical/metasurface testing via `test_demo.test_physical()` and `_optimize_phi_gd()` from `teacher_experiments.py`.

Keep this rule centered on the ordinary teacher path. GAN classes also exist in `teacher.py`, but they are a separate channel-modeling path and should only be considered for GAN-specific tasks.

## Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `teacher.py` | Current teacher focus: `MyTeacher`, encoder, learned linear channel, decoder, GAN helpers; also `ThinTeacher` ablation model |
| `teacher_train.py` | Teacher training functions, including `train_teacher_linear()` |
| `test_demo.py` | Physical/metasurface testing (`test_physical()`) plus the GAN-channel test (`test_physical_channel_gan()`); re-exports `noise()` from `gan.gan` |
| `teacher_experiments.py` | Phase/metasurface optimization helpers (`_optimize_phi_gd()`, `get_channel_matching_loss()`, etc.) and alternate teachers (`HeavyIntermediateTeacher`, `MNISTClassifier`, `E2EProxyTeacher`) |
| `students.py` | Student model definitions |
| `channels.py` | Channel generation (`generate_channel_tensors_by_type`) |
| `training.py` | All training functions |
| `CLI_interface.py` | CLI entry point for all training phases |
